v 3
d ctools: C-accelerated tools for Stata
d
d ctools is a set of really fast drop-in replacements for a variety
d of Stata programs. All of the numerical heavy lifting for each
d command is implemented in highly optimized C.
d
d Included commands:
d   csort           - Parallel sorting (IPS4o, radix, timsort, etc.)
d   cmerge          - C-accelerated dataset merging
d   cimport         - Delimited text, Excel, and binary statistical file import
d   cexport         - Delimited text, Excel, and binary statistical file export
d   creghdfe        - HDFE regression with CG solver
d   civreghdfe      - IV/2SLS regression with HDFE
d   cqreg           - Quantile regression with IPM solver
d   cbinscatter     - Binned scatter plots
d   cencode/cdecode - Convert value labels
d   cdestring       - Convert strings to numeric data
d   csample/cbsample - Sampling and bootstrap draws
d   cwinsor         - Winsorize or trim variables
d   crangestat      - Range statistics
d   cinterpolate    - Linear and cubic interpolation
d   csplit          - String splitting
d   crangejoin      - Interval joins
d   cgeonear        - Nearest neighbors and geodetic distances
d   cjoinby         - All pairwise combinations within groups
d   creshape        - Reshape between wide and long form
d   cfuzzyjoin      - Fuzzy record linkage, similarity joins, string groups
d   csql            - SQL queries on data and files, through DuckDB
d   cdistinct       - Distinct value counts
d   cegen           - Extensions to generate (egen functions)
d   ccollapse       - Summary statistics by group
d   cpsmatch        - Propensity score matching (ATT)
d   cppmlhdfe       - PPML with high-dimensional fixed effects
d   chdfe           - Partial out high-dimensional fixed effects
d
d Version: 1.4.0
d
d Requires: Stata 14.1 or later
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261127

